@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a plain string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    >>> console.out("Hello", "World!")
+
+Unlike print, out does not pretty print objects, wrap or crop output, process console markup, or replace emoji codes. Output is written as plain text with an optional basic ``style``. Highlighting is applied by default; pass ``highlight=False`` to turn it off, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's default setting.
+
+
